{
  "id": "connectionist-model",
  "term": "connectionist model",
  "definition": "A connectionist model is a computational approach that explains behavior as the result of interacting processes that change over time. In this packet, it refers to a dynamic model of intertemporal choice used to represent how factors such as self-control and the way time is framed jointly shape decisions between sooner smaller rewards and later larger rewards.",
